  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Readers can give preferences on a shared request sheet, and staff can reserve space in several pickup windows.\", \"decision\": \"How should readers and staff agree on pickup windows?\", \"goal\": \"Keep books moving and make the afternoon service easier to use without excluding readers who arrive without an appointment.\", \"problem\": \"A small library becomes crowded during afternoon pickups and returns. It has a request sheet, adjustable pickup windows, a few trained helpers, labeled shelves, and enough room to separate several activities. Staff want a practical plan that preserves walk-in access. Each decision below concerns a different part of the service; none requires exclusive use of all helpers or space.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nReaders claim pickup windows on the request sheet while staff reserve shelf space as claims arrive. The available spaces limit crowding as readers make their own choices.\nReaders rank pickup windows on the request sheet before staff reserve shelf space. Staff can use those preferences to spread pickups across the available windows.\nStaff propose pickup windows on the request sheet before readers confirm or request a change. The initial spread comes from staff, with reader preferences correcting unsuitable assignments."
    }
